From 1efb1faf6926221cdfc64465e317c2f5c7e98141 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Thompson <brandon.joseph.thompson@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:31:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] hwpstate_amd(4): Backport CPPC support from main

Take sys/x86/cpufreq/hwpstate_amd.c from main as of 1a3d61552546
("hwpstate_amd(4): Restore CPU ID cache after introducing
cpu_get_pcpuid()"), which drives Zen CPUs through CPPC with per-CPU
EPP and min/max/desired performance knobs instead of the few legacy
P-states.

15.1 lacks two helpers main grew, cpu_get_pcpuid() and
smp_rendezvous_cpu(); define them locally rather than touch sys/cpu.h
and subr_smp.c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
